* Week 8: BAL is built entirely from NOTANY and ARBNO -- no hand-written
* paren-depth counter (research/snobol/03-pattern-matching.md, worked
* example 2: "(A(B)C)DE)" unanchored, BAL matches "(A(B)C)"). BAL is the
* shortest *nonnull* balanced string, so it stops at the first fully
* balanced prefix rather than continuing on into "DE)", which would
* leave an unmatched trailing paren.
        SUBJECT = '(A(B)C)DE)'
        SUBJECT BAL             :F(NOMATCH)
        OUTPUT = 'BAL MATCHED'         :(STOP)
NOMATCH OUTPUT = 'NO MATCH'
STOP    SUBJECT = SUBJECT
